 average), Wednesday surge_index=1.2723 (27.2% above average), Saturday surge_index=1.2632 (26.3% above average). These elevate surge risks.\nRed Velvet Powder: Tuesday surge_index=1.4578 (45.8% above average), Saturday surge_index=1.3373 (33.7% above average). These elevate surge risks.\nStrawberry Jam: Saturday surge_index=1.3848 (38.5% above average), Wednesday surge_index=1.2291 (22.9% above average). These elevate surge risks.\n\nPROCUREMENT DIRECTIVES:\nAssam Black Tea: IMMEDIATE ACTION REQUIRED - Order 155180.95 ml\nFresh Milk: IMMEDIATE ACTION REQUIRED - Order 84334.52 ml\nFructose: IMMEDIATE ACTION REQUIRED - Order 30084.38 ml\nNon-Dairy Creamer (NDC): IMMEDIATE ACTION REQUIRED - Order 15823.27 g\nMatcha Powder: IMMEDIATE ACTION REQUIRED - Order 14086.02 g\nFrappe Base: IMMEDIATE ACTION REQUIRED - Order 12373.52 g\nStrawberry Powder: IMMEDIATE ACTION REQUIRED - Order 9717.62 g\nMango Powder: IMMEDIATE ACTION REQUIRED - Order 9049.04 g\nCheesecake Walling: IMMEDIATE ACTION REQUIRED - Order 6008.73 g\nCoffee Powder: IMMEDIATE ACTION REQUIRED - Order 5978.24 g\nCookies & Cream Powder: IMMEDIATE ACTION REQUIRED - Order 5871.90 g\nNata de Coco: IMMEDIATE ACTION REQUIRED - Order 4373.53 g\nCondensed Milk: PRIORITY ORDER WITHIN 48 HOURS - Order 4086.20 ml\nOreo Crumbs: PRIORITY ORDER WITHIN 48 HOURS - Order 3965.25 g\nMilk Choco Powder: PRIORITY ORDER WITHIN 48 HOURS - Order 3919.34 g\nWhipped Cream: PRIORITY ORDER WITHIN 48 HOURS - Order 3976.72 g\nChoco Syrup: PRIORITY ORDER WITHIN 48 HOURS - Order 3628.38 ml\nBlueberry Powder: PRIORITY ORDER WITHIN 48 HOURS - Order 3258.57 g\nGraham Crumbs: PRIORITY ORDER WITHIN 48 HOURS - Order 3179.50 g\nHoney: PRIORITY ORDER WITHIN 48 HOURS - Order 3192.15 ml\nLemon Syrup: PRIORITY ORDER WITHIN 48 HOURS - Order 3192.15 ml\nDark Choco Powder: PRIORITY ORDER WITHIN 48 HOURS - Order 2961.34 g\nTaro Powder: PRIORITY ORDER WITHIN 48 HOURS - Order 1790.67 g\nCaramel Syrup: PRIORITY ORDER WITHIN 48 HOURS - Order 1714.90 ml\nRed Velvet Powder: PRIORITY ORDER WITHIN 48 HOURS - Order 1719.33 g\nStrawberry Jam: PRIORITY ORDER WITHIN 48 HOURS - Order 1455.40 ml','2026-05-17 12:12:14'),(4,'financial','EXECUTIVE SUMMARY:\nThis week, Net Profit decreased to PHP 14,294.78 from PHP 15,664.90 last week, alongside a reduction in Gross Sales to PHP 21,673.00 from PHP 24,456.00, indicating that the business is currently shrinking.\n\nMARGIN & COGS ANALYSIS:\nThe Food Cost Margin for this week stands at 34.04% (PHP 7,378.22 COGS / PHP 21,673.00 Gross Sales), which is well within the healthy target range of 30%-35%. Last week\'s margin was 34.10%. This demonstrates consistent and efficient spending on cost of goods sold relative to sales volume, even as sales have declined.\n\nOPERATIONAL LEAKS:\nThis week, there were zero peso amounts lost to Store Expenses and Z-Reading Variance. This marks a significant improvement from last week, which saw PHP 450.00 lost to Store Expenses and PHP 841.00 lost to Z-Reading Variance.\n\nCFO RECOMMENDATION:\nGiven the 11.38% decrease in Gross Sales this week, it is imperative to implement a targeted marketing or promotional campaign immediately to drive customer traffic and revenue back towards last week\'s levels or higher.','2026-05-17 12:12:21'),(5,'auditor','SECURITY ALERT: IMMEDIATE ACTION REQUIRED\n\n*   Two transactions totaling ₱236.00 were voided yesterday. While no cash variance was recorded, this high frequency and total value of voids in a single shift constitutes suspicious activity and requires immediate investigation.\n*   Admin must review CCTV footage for 2026-05-16 at 03:32 AM (Void ID 3994) and 04:30 AM (Void ID 3988) to determine the exact circumstances and personnel involved.','2026-05-17 12:12:29'),(6,'forecaster','Subject: Urgent: TriSync Inventory Status Update - Critical Stock Levels Identified by AI Analysis\n\nDear [Business Owner Name],\n\nEXECUTIVE SUMMARY:\nI\'m writing to you today with an urgent update on our current inventory levels, following our AI\'s latest 180-day data analysis. The system has identified 12 critical ingredients that are on the verge of stockout within the next 7 days, and an additional 14 items that are rapidly approaching risk levels.\n\nSTRATEGIC INVENTORY INSIGHTS:\nOur AI-powered Exponentially Weighted Moving Average model has provided invaluable insights into our supply chain health, highlighting several areas that require immediate attention.\n\nFirstly, our Assam Black Tea supply is in a critically precarious position. Its current burn rate is exceptionally high at over 4371 ml per day, meaning our existing stock of 1000 ml will be depleted within a day. What\'s concerning is that our recent consumption trend shows a slight increase, and we\'re heading into a weekend with anticipated demand spikes of 37% on Saturday and 27% on Sunday. Without an immediate order, we will undoubtedly run out, impacting our most popular tea-based beverages.\n\nSimilarly, Fresh Milk is also facing an immediate stockout within the next day. While its demand momentum has seen a 15.2% decline over the past 30 days, its sheer volume of use remains incredibly high at over 2386 ml daily. With only 1000 ml currently in stock, and knowing that Sundays typically see a 31% surge in demand, followed by Saturdays with a 27% spike, our current supply will not even last through tomorrow\'s service. We simply cannot operate without this staple.\n\nLastly, Strawberry Powder is another item demanding our strategic attention. We are observing a significant 27.8% upward trend in demand for this ingredient. This strong positive momentum indicates a rapidly growing popularity, suggesting it\'s becoming a key favorite among our customers. With our current stock projected to last only four more days, and considering the typical weekend spikes (33% on Saturday, 26% on Sunday), we risk disappointing a growing segment of our customer base very soon if we don\'t replenish.\n\nPROCUREMENT ACTION PLAN:\nTo mitigate immediate stockout risks and ensure business continuity, I recommend approving the following emergency procurement orders:\n\nIngredient: Assam Black Tea | Recommended Order: 155180.95 ml\nIngredient: Fresh Milk | Recommended Order: 84334.52 ml\nIngredient: Fructose | Recommended Order: 30084.38 ml\nIngredient: Non-Dairy Creamer (NDC) | Recommended Order: 15823.27 g\nIngredient: Matcha Powder | Recommended Order: 14086.02 g\nIngredient: Frappe Base | Recommended Order: 12373.52 g\nIngredient: Strawberry Powder | Recommended Order: 9717.62 g\nIngredient: Mango Powder | Recommended Order: 9049.04 g\nIngredient: Cheesecake Walling | Recommended Order: 6008.73 g\nIngredient: Coffee Powder | Recommended Order: 5978.24 g\nIngredient: Cookies & Cream Powder | Recommended Order: 5871.90 g\nIngredient: Nata de Coco | Recommended Order: 4373.53 g\nIngredient: Condensed Milk | Recommended Order: 4086.20 ml\nIngredient: Oreo Crumbs | Recommended Order: 3965.25 g\nIngredient: Milk Choco Powder | Recommended Order: 3919.34 g\nIngredient: Whipped Cream | Recommended Order: 3976.72 g\nIngredient: Choco Syrup | Recommended Order: 3628.38 ml\nIngredient: Blueberry Powder | Recommended Order: 3258.57 g\nIngredient: Graham Crumbs | Recommended Order: 3179.50 g\nIngredient: Honey | Recommended Order: 3192.15 ml\nIngredient: Lemon Syrup | Recommended Order: 3192.15 ml\nIngredient: Dark Choco Powder | Recommended Order: 2961.34 g\nIngredient: Taro Powder | Recommended Order: 1790.67 g\nIngredient: Caramel Syrup | Recommended Order: 1714.90 ml\nIngredient: Red Velvet Powder | Recommended Order: 1719.33 g\nIngredient: Strawberry Jam | Recommended Order: 1455.40 ml\n\nDATA TO ANALYZE:\n[Ingredient: Assam Black Tea] | Status: CRITICAL | Stock: 1000 ml\nCurrent Burn Rate: 4371.08/day (7-day trend: 4402.25, 30-day baseline: 4318.69)\nDemand Momentum: 1.9%\nWeekend Surge Risk: YES | Surge Days: Saturday (37% spike), Sunday (27% spike)\nProjected 7-Day Demand: 30597.16 | Stockout Expected: Day 1\nRecomme