s week\nRecommended Order: 1485.99 ml','2026-05-18 02:15:26'),(16,'auditor','Dear Business Owner,\n\nThis brief provides an update from our daily loss prevention review concerning yesterday\'s activity. We observed one voided transaction during operating hours, with no corresponding cash variance reported. While the till balanced, the specifics of this void transaction require your immediate attention.\n\nThe transaction in question, identified by ID 4036 and timestamped 2026-05-18T06:14:10Z, was processed for a voided amount of ₱101.14. However, upon reviewing the item details within this void, which included two Strawberry & Cream Frappes and an Extra Oreo Crumbs modifier, the actual product value totals ₱108.00. This ₱6.86 discrepancy between the voided amount and the actual item value is a significant concern. I strongly recommend that you personally review the CCTV footage of the cashier station for 2026-05-18 at precisely 06:14:10Z. Furthermore, it is critical to speak directly with the cashier on duty at that exact time to understand the reasons behind this particular void and the inconsistency in the recorded amount.','2026-05-19 02:00:12'),(17,'forecaster','Subject: Urgent: Critical Inventory Update - Action Required Based on AI-Powered Demand Forecast\n\nEXECUTIVE SUMMARY:\nGood morning, [Owner\'s Name]. Our latest AI-powered analysis of 180 days of historical data provides a clear, urgent picture of our inventory health. The model highlights 11 items currently at critical stock levels with immediate stockout risk, alongside another 11 items approaching warning thresholds.\n\nSTRATEGIC INVENTORY INSIGHTS:\nThe data reveals several critical areas demanding immediate attention to prevent significant operational disruptions and lost sales, particularly as we approach the weekend.\n\nAssam Black Tea and Fresh Milk are our most pressing concerns. Despite the AI model indicating a slight negative momentum in overall demand for both (meaning the rate of growth has slowed), their sheer daily consumption rates are far exceeding our current stock. We are effectively out of both Assam Black Tea and Fresh Milk as of today, meaning we cannot fulfill current daily demand, let alone absorb the significant weekend surges we typically experience (up to 38% for Assam on Saturday, and 31% for Fresh Milk on Sunday). This isn\'t just about running low; it\'s about being unable to serve core menu items starting now.\n\nOn a more positive note regarding demand, Strawberry Powder is showing a healthy 5.2% upward trend in popularity, indicating growing customer preference. However, this positive momentum, combined with its consistent daily burn rate, means our current 1000g stock is only projected to last until the end of Day 4. With expected weekend spikes, we need to proactively secure supply for this growing favorite to prevent a stockout precisely when demand peaks.\n\nPROCUREMENT ACTION PLAN:\nBased on these insights and the AI model\'s recommendations, I strongly recommend we approve the immediate procurement of the following critical items:\n\nAssam Black Tea: 126269.01 ml\nFresh Milk: 69761.77 ml\nFructose: 24491.23 ml\nNon-Dairy Creamer (NDC): 12693.36 g\nMatcha Powder: 11364.78 g\nFrappe Base: 9855.81 g\nStrawberry Powder: 8039.96 g\nMango Powder: 7264.06 g\nCoffee Powder: 4679.97 g\nCheesecake Walling: 4605.80 g\nCookies & Cream Powder: 4416.45 g\n\nDATA TO ANALYZE:\n[Ingredient: Assam Black Tea] | Status: CRITICAL | Stock: 1000 ml\nCurrent Burn Rate: 3560.24/day (7-day trend: 3248.01, 30-day baseline: 4019.32)\nDemand Momentum: -19.2%\nWeekend Surge Risk: YES | Surge Days: Saturday (38% spike), Sunday (28% spike)\nProjected 7-Day Demand: 24922.06 | Stockout Expected: Day 1\nRecommended Order: 126269.01 ml\n\n[Ingredient: Fresh Milk] | Status: CRITICAL | Stock: 1000 ml\nCurrent Burn Rate: 1974.83/day (7-day trend: 1658.31, 30-day baseline: 2447.47)\nDemand Momentum: -32.2%\nWeekend Surge Risk: YES | Surge Days: Sunday (31% spike),