 Syrup] | Status: WARNING | Stock: 1000 ml\nCurrent Burn Rate: 96.80/day (7-day trend: 87.42, 30-day baseline: 111.48)\nDemand Momentum: -21.6%\nWeekend Surge Risk: YES | Surge Days: Saturday (57% spike), Sunday (20% spike)\nProjected 7-Day Demand: 677.60 | Stockout Expected: Not this week\nRecommended Order: 2456.47 ml\n\n[Ingredient: Graham Crumbs] | Status: WARNING | Stock: 1000 g\nCurrent Burn Rate: 96.59/day (7-day trend: 94.46, 30-day baseline: 99.61)\nDemand Momentum: -5.2%\nWeekend Surge Risk: YES | Surge Days: Sunday (58% spike), Saturday (46% spike)\nProjected 7-Day Demand: 676.14 | Stockout Expected: Not this week\nRecommended Order: 2447.32 g\n\n[Ingredient: Dark Choco Powder] | Status: WARNING | Stock: 1000 g\nCurrent Burn Rate: 90.08/day (7-day trend: 77.24, 30-day baseline: 105.21)\nDemand Momentum: -26.6%\nWeekend Surge Risk: YES | Surge Days: Sunday (56% spike)\nProjected 7-Day Demand: 630.53 | Stockout Expected: Not this week\nRecommended Order: 2214.80 g','2026-05-19 02:15:22'),(18,'forecaster','Subject: Urgent: Critical Inventory Update and Immediate Procurement Recommendations\n\nEXECUTIVE SUMMARY:\nGood morning, [Owner\'s Name]. I\'m writing to you with an urgent update on our inventory situation. Our latest AI-powered EWMA analysis, leveraging 180 days of historical data, has identified 8 critical items that are projected to run out within the week, alongside 14 additional items at risk of depletion soon after.\n\nSTRATEGIC INVENTORY INSIGHTS:\nUpon reviewing the model\'s output, several key items require our immediate attention. While we\'ve observed a general softening in demand momentum across many ingredients over the past 30 days, our current stock levels are simply too low to absorb current consumption and the predictable weekend surges.\n\nFresh Milk is our most immediate concern, projected to run out today. Despite the overall demand trend for milk having softened by nearly 46% over recent weeks, our current inventory of 1000 ml is drastically insufficient to meet even one day\'s standard sales, let alone the significant 29-32% spikes we typically experience on Saturdays and Sundays. We simply don\'t have enough on hand to cover the immediate consumption.\n\nSimilarly, our Assam Black Tea, a core ingredient for many popular drinks, is on track to be depleted by day 4. While its month-over-month demand trend shows a mild softening of about 35%, the consistently high daily consumption, combined with the nearly 40% spike we anticipate this Saturday, means our existing stock will be quickly exhausted. We need to act swiftly to avoid disrupting our most popular tea-based offerings.\n\nMango Powder also presents a significant risk, expected to run out by day 5. Although its demand trend is down by around 37%, its popularity during weekend rushes, especially with a massive 63% spike on Sundays, will rapidly consume our limited supply. We want to ensure we don\'t miss out on those peak sales opportunities for mango-flavored items, particularly with the upcoming weekend.\n\nPROCUREMENT ACTION PLAN:\nTo mitigate these immediate risks and ensure continuity of our key product offerings, I recommend approving the following orders:\n\nCritical Items for immediate replenishment:\n1. Fresh Milk: 57774.56 ml\n2. Fructose: 19908.94 ml\n3. Non-Dairy Creamer (NDC): 9903.90 g\n4. Assam Black Tea: 95347.72 ml\n5. Matcha Powder: 9146.02 g\n6. Frappe Base: 7540.79 g\n7. Mango Powder: 5892.93 g\n8. Strawberry Powder: 5936.18 g\n\nAdditional items to proactively order to prevent future stockouts:\n9. Coffee Powder: 3695.49 g\n10. Cheesecake Walling: 3581.04 g\n11. Cookies & Cream Powder: 3422.11 g\n12. Nata de Coco: 2724.54 g\n13. Condensed Milk: 2422.11 ml\n14. Milk Choco Powder: 2396.52 g\n15. Oreo Crumbs: 2328.20 g\n16. Choco Syrup: 2098.34 ml\n17. Whipped Cream: 2227.53 g\n18. Blueberry Powder: 1888.18 g\n19. Honey: 1839.67 ml\n20. Lemon Syrup: 1839.67 ml\n21. Graham Crumbs: 1846.42 g\n22. Dark Choco Powder: 1685.66 g\n\nPlease let me know if you have any questions or require further details. Your prompt approval on these orders is crucial to maintaining our service levels and revenue.\n\nBest regards,\n\n[Your Name]\nTriSync Supply Chain Director','2026-05-20 02:15:16');
